  id: liminal-doors-phone-booth
  displayName: Liminal Doors phone booth
  kind: prop
  version: 1.0.0
  description: 'The pink K6 phone booth at the start of Liminal Doors: a bevelled
    cast-iron kiosk in hot pink enamel with chipped edges and weathering, lit butter-yellow
    TELEPHONE signs, gilded crowns, a brass door pull, pink glass with fingerprints,
    and a payphone inside with a chrome keypad, handset and coiled cord. Gold and
    pink sparkles swirl up around it.'
  forPC: 1
  forAndroid: 0
  moves: 0
  prefab: {fileID: 3133622112822875829, guid: f0a430abc6953124787b48dc69e07529, type: 3}
  maxTriangles: 30000
  maxMaterials: 5
  maxTextureSize: 2048
  maxParticles: 400
  creator: Astra (built with Claude)
  source: Modelled in Blender by Tools/Blender/make_phone_booth.py after Sir Giles
    Gilbert Scott's K6 kiosk (proportions only); textures baked there from CC0 ambientCG
    scans; sparkles and prefab made in Liminal Doors
  license: own-work
  attribution: 'Surface scans: ambientCG.com PaintedMetal002, Metal009, Smear002,
    Scratches001 (CC0; credit not required)'
  publicOk: 1
  changelog: '1.0.0: first version. Handmade K6 booth modelled in Blender (bevels,
    recessed posts, narrow-wide-narrow glazing, lit TELEPHONE signs, gilded crowns,
    dome, brass pull); baked ambient occlusion, edge wear, grime, rain streaks and
    sun fade over CC0 scans; our own Unity Stable/Handmade PBR (clear coat, world-space
    scan detail); the payphone on a panel built into the back wall, with chrome keypad,
    instruction card, coin slots, handset and coiled cord; pink glass with fingerprints
    (Unity Stable Pink Glass); gold and pink sparkles swirling up around it (Unity
    Stable Sparkle); gold base glow.'
